.TH CHTTP_BASIC_AUTH 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_basic_auth \- build an HTTP Basic auth header value (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

char *chttp_basic_auth(const char *username, const char *password);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a static inline wrapper around chttp_basic_auth_mp(). It gives
NULL for the memory management procedures, so the function uses malloc
and free.

RFC 7617 SS2 makes the colon the one delimiter of the encoded
"user-id:password" string. A recipient cuts that string at its FIRST
colon. A username with a colon in it is therefore not transmittable
without ambiguity, and the function rejects it. Without that
rejection, the username "a:b" with the password "c" encodes to the
same bytes as the username "a" with the password "b:c". A caller that
asks for one identity therefore sends a different one. A colon in the
password needs no escape, and the function builds the string as the
caller asks.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
username  The username. It must not be NULL. It can be empty. It must
          not contain a colon (':').
password  The password. It must not be NULL. It can be empty. It can
          contain colons.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new "Basic <base64>" string, if the call succeeds.
NULL, if the allocation fails, if username or password is NULL, or if
username contains a colon.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_basic_auth_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode (3)
